   "definition_quote": "At every time $t\\in [T]$, each noncorrupted agent $i\\in\\cN_0^t$ is presented with a decision set $\\cD_i^t\\subseteq\\mathbb{R}^d$. It selects an action $x_i^t$ from $\\cD_i^t$ and receives a reward $r_i^t=\\langle x_i^t, \\theta^\\ast\\rangle + \\eta_i^t$... Assume at least half of the agents are consistently reliable, i.e., $\\alpha \\triangleq N_1 / N < 1/2$."
